From 773ad40748faae9a76d1b24f9304558c1c24a33e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SMARK <3222301373@qq.com>
Date: Sat, 23 May 2026 06:26:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?feat:=20=E4=B8=B2=E8=81=94=E4=BF=AE=E6=AD=A3aut?=
 =?UTF-8?q?o=E8=B7=AF=E7=94=B1=E9=80=BB=E8=BE=91=20Enhance=20permission=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?handling=20for=20shell=20commands=20and=20external=20directory?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20access?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Capture optional collaborators during Permission.Service construction to improve context resolution.
- Refactor permission evaluation logic to streamline auto-review processes, ensuring sensitive operations are routed correctly.
- Introduce deterministic precheck for external directory access initiated by shell commands, preventing unnecessary user prompts.
- Update reviewer policies to explicitly deny direct reads of sensitive files and improve handling of PowerShell commands.
- Add comprehensive tests for new permission routing behaviors, including handling of SSH keys and user profile credential reads.
- Ensure that non-shell commands maintain existing user approval paths while allowing shell commands to leverage auto-review capabilities.

